<title>LEBANON: Saudi Lebanese Bank 1996 profits up.</title>
<headline>Saudi Lebanese Bank 1996 profits up.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Lebanese Bank announced a 182 percent rise in net profits in 1996 in consolidated results published in newspapers on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Profits were 12.48 billion Lebanese pounds ($8.04 million) from 4.42 billion pounds in 1995.</p>
<p>Assets increased 15 percent to 673 billion pounds, customer deposits rose 18.9 percent to 503 billion pounds and capital was unchanged at 20 billion pounds, the bank said.</p>
<p>Saudi Lebanese Bank has five branches in Lebanon and 149 employees, according to the almanac of the Lebanese Banks Association.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following results (in billions of Lebanese pounds):</p>
<p>			     1996		1995</p>
<p>    Net profits	 12.480	     4.425</p>
<p>    Assets	   673.054	   584.836</p>
<p>    Deposits	   502.888	   422.846</p>
<p>Loans &amp;</p>
<p>    Advances	   306.499	   255.143</p>
<p>    Capital	     20.00	     20.00</p>
<p>($1 = 1,552 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/96)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 345723 345740 602057</p>
